In `CODEOWNERS`, inline comments starting with `#` are allowed. The current implementation only checks if the line starts with `#`. If there is an inline comment (e.g., `* @owner # comment`), the `#` and subsequent words will be parsed as owners, leading to incorrect owners like `#`, `comment`, etc. We should strip comments from the line before parsing.

```suggestion
    for line in codeowners.splitlines():
        line = line.split("#", 1)[0].strip()
        if not line:
            continue
        for tok in line.split()[1:]:
            _add(tok)
```
